{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Contributor-triggerable re-review: a `recheck-review` comment re-runs any LLM-Review that is not a real finding\n\n## Problem\n\nAn `LLM-Review -1` has two different meanings and only one contributor response: a **real\nfinding** (`[LLM-Review: BLOCK — finding]`) is fixed by amending; every OTHER `-1` — the\ncoverage-gap family (`gate-disabled`, `llm-unavailable`, `scanner`, `review-error`,\n`indeterminate`, `merge-review`), including a retry-budget escalation from ticket\n0347-b2cc-e6e9-4f6b — is an infrastructure veto the contributor can do nothing about.\nToday the only remedies are an operator-run `/rerun` (SSM-token-gated; see\n`infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md`) or amending to spin a new patchset. CI already gives\ncontributors `recheck` for a `Verified -1` flake; the LLM lane has no equivalent. This\nmirrors the OSS norm (Zuul/OpenStack `recheck`, Prow `/retest`) with one deliberate\nrestriction: LLM reviewers are stochastic, so retrying a REAL finding would be dice-rolled\nself-approval — the retry surface must exclude findings.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Trigger surface: a Gerrit comment containing `recheck-review`** (its own token —\n`recheck` stays CI's). Wire it end to end:\n\n1. **Event plumbing** — `infra/gerrit/webhooks.config` gains `event = comment-added`\n   alongside `patchset-created` (the plugin sends only listed types). Note in the file +\n   ticket comment: an operator must re-run `infra/gerrit/service-user.sh` to push the\n   rendered config to `refs/meta/config` before the trigger goes live; until then the\n   code path is inert (no events arrive).\n2. **Routing** — the receiver's `/webhook` already enqueues every payload; the worker\n   (`app.py::_worker`) routes `type == \"comment-added\"` to a NEW module\n   `src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py` (voter.py is at ~670/800 LOC post-0347; this is a\n   separate concern and its own seam) instead of `review_and_vote`. All other types keep\n   the existing path.\n3. **`retrigger.handle_comment_added(event, config, gerrit, dedup)`** does, in order:\n   - **Loop guard**: ignore comments authored by the bot itself (`cfg.bot_user`), else the\n     bot's own replies re-trigger events forever.\n   - **Token match**: the comment text must contain `recheck-review` (word match, not\n     substring of another word); anything else is a silent skip.\n   - **Eligibility — decided privileged-side from durable Gerrit state, never from the\n     requesting comment**: fetch the bot's latest change message for the CURRENT revision\n     and parse its first-line tag (the `_TAG_SUFFIXES` vocabulary, test-asserted). The\n     ONLY ineligible state is a current-revision `[LLM-Review: BLOCK — finding]` tag: a\n     real finding is refused — fix and re-push. Everything else is eligible: every\n     coverage-gap sub-reason (including `merge-review` and a 0347 retries-exhausted\n     escalation), a PASS (a fresh review can only produce a fresh verdict — it can flip\n     PASS to BLOCK, which is fail-closed-safe, and never mints an unearned PASS), and a\n     vote-less change (harmless: equivalent to a reconciler re-drive).\n   - **On refusal**: post a short reply comment (a message, never a vote) telling the\n     contributor the `-1` is a real finding and the path is amend + re-push; emit a\n     greppable `RETRIGGER_REFUSED` log marker.\n   - **On acceptance**: `dedup.reset_attempts(change_id, current_revision)` (the 0347\n     budget DELETE — the shared-budget harmonization: the human trigger re-arms the\n     bounded automatic retries), enqueue the change's current revision with the existing\n     `_rebar_force` marker (the `/rerun` force path — bypasses dedup + existing-vote\n     short-circuits, still fail-closed), post a short \"re-review queued\" reply, and emit\n     `RETRIGGER_ACCEPTED`.\n4. **Harmonize `/rerun`** — the operator endpoint also resets the attempts budget before\n   enqueueing (today it would force a review that could immediately re-escalate on a\n   stale budget). `/rerun` keeps its unrestricted semantics (an operator may force even a\n   finding re-review); the finding-refusal applies only to the contributor comment path.\n5. **Gerrit client** — add the two small REST calls `retrigger` needs if absent: latest\n   bot change message for a revision, and post-comment-without-vote (post_vote with\n   value 0 or the bare `/review` message form, whichever the API offers cleanly).\n\n### Security property (must be tested, not just implemented)\n\nA `recheck-review` comment on a change whose current revision carries a findings-BLOCK\ndoes NOT enqueue a review, does NOT reset the budget, and does NOT touch the vote —\nasserted by a dedicated test. Also asserted: the bot's own comments never trigger, and a\nnon-matching comment is a no-op. The trigger can only ever request a FRESH review through\nthe same fail-closed pipeline; nothing in this path writes a vote directly.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `infra/gerrit/webhooks.config` — `event = comment-added`.\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py` (new) — routing target, eligibility, replies.\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/app.py` — worker routes `comment-added` to `retrigger`; `/rerun`\n  gains the budget reset.\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py` — message-fetch / comment-post helpers if absent.\n- `docs/review-policy.md` — the coverage-gap rows' \"Your productive response\" becomes\n  \"comment `recheck-review`\"; document the finding refusal.\n- `CONTRIBUTING.md` §2c — mention `recheck-review` beside `recheck`.\n- `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` — note the contributor path; `/rerun` stays the\n  operator escape hatch.\n- Tests in `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py` (worker routing) and a new\n  `tests/unit/test_review_bot_retrigger.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: a `recheck-review` comment on a change whose current-revision tag is any\n      coverage-gap sub-reason resets the attempts budget, enqueues a forced re-review,\n      and posts the \"queued\" reply — asserted by tests (at least gate-disabled and a\n      retries-exhausted escalation case).\n- [ ] AC2 (security property): the same comment on a findings-BLOCK revision is refused —\n      no enqueue, no budget reset, no vote change, refusal reply posted,\n      `RETRIGGER_REFUSED` emitted — asserted by a dedicated test.\n- [ ] AC3: comments by the bot itself and comments without the token are no-ops (no\n      reply, no enqueue) — asserted by tests.\n- [ ] AC4: `/rerun` resets the attempts budget before enqueueing — asserted by a test.\n- [ ] AC5: `webhooks.config` lists `comment-added`; the file's comment and the runbook\n      state that `service-user.sh` must be re-run to activate it.\n- [ ] AC6: `docs/review-policy.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md` §2c document `recheck-review`\n      (incl. the finding refusal).\n- [ ] AC7: `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the review-bot test modules pass; every\n      touched/new `src/rebar` module stays within the 800-LOC cap (new module ≥100 LOC).\n\n## Testing / Verification\n\nFrom the worktree venv:\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot.py tests/unit/test_review_bot_retrigger.py -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`\n\n## Relationship to 0347\n\nLands AFTER 0347-b2cc-e6e9-4f6b (this ticket consumes its `review_attempts` ledger and\n`reset_attempts` DELETE semantics). 0347 handles the automatic recovery (vote-less defer +\nbounded escalation); this ticket is the human escape hatch that re-arms it once the\nunderlying failure is corrected.","title":"Contributor recheck-review comment re-runs any LLM-Review that is not a real finding"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785704672075075001,"uuid":"70e43e92-b9fb-4286-9294-bd7d4c096570"}